// Mach-O - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// Mach-O: Apple's executable format, and a header of seven
// four-byte fields -- magic, cputype, cpusubtype, filetype,
// ncmds, sizeofcmds, flags.
//
// The magic is the constant FEEDFACE written in the *file's* byte
// order, which is why there are four magics and not one. Reading
// the magic wrong way round reads every field after it as a
// byte-swapped number and still succeeds, which is why the
// checker reports the endianness it chose.
//
// filetype 2 is MH_EXECUTE. ncmds is 1 rather than 0, because a
// header with no load commands is a relocatable object.
//
// Hello World! is in the comment above and nowhere in the header,
// because a Mach-O header has no field for prose.
//
// macho: 28 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// CE FA ED FE 07 00 00 01 03 00 00 00 02 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0000
// 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 85 00 00 00             |............|   <- 0010
